OK, you've done Soko so you should have plenty of food. That's good.
That means you can slow down, there's no rush to explore the rest of
the dungeon for food. Altar camp for a while if you feel like it,
especially if you have a source of create monster.

Your AC isn't bad but it could probably be better. Scrolls of EA are
great, but your best source of AC right now is from pre-enchanted
armour. Have you BUC-tested and tried on every (studded) leather armour
yet? One of them might be +4, you never know. Might be worth trying on
some other armour too, maybe a small shield or some headgear. Keep an
eye on your spell failure rates, you may decide that a slight
compromise on failure rate justifies a boost in AC. Crystal mail is
good if you can find it and can stand the weight (avoid being
burdened). If you have no gloves, it might be worth training your pet
up until it's ready to kill the minetown watch. That's at least one
extra AC point right there. Be careful not to lose your pet: A
stethoscope and healing spell are handy here.If you've already lost
your pet, get a new one.
Oh, and you might be surprised about buying protection. Empty a few
vaults (rummaging around with a pickaxe is also a good way to pick up
teleport scrolls, btw) and you might find you have enought to donate.
This burns food though, so be careful. Bones files often have tons of
cash too. Ludios is probably a bit out of your league until you beef
yourself up a bit.

It's probably be worth destroying the statues on the oracle level with
force bolt/pickaxe, there might be some spellbooks there for you. Get
all spellbooks back to the altar before reading them, and don't read
the cursed ones.

Keep an eye out for chances to acquire poison resistance, or any other
resistances, they can negate a great many instadeaths. Shriekers are
yummy.

Have you got magicbane and a good stack of daggers yet? You need to be
working on that, and practising your dagger skill. Get that up to
expert asap. Forget the quarterstaff. Magicbane is probably your top
priority. Altar camp for it, then (carefully) start exploring deeper
into the mines or the main dungeon- whichever looks least threatening.
Don't go into dark mines without a light source (or liberal casting of
the "light" spell). Remember to retreat often to heal up, and keep an
eye on your Pow- as a wizard you rely upon it.

You're doing well. Don't let yourself get cornered without means of
escape, don't do anything stupid and you could be in for a good game.



